\paragraph{(P2) Candidate model equations per stage.}
The outcome law of each block is given where the stage is introduced: the pattern law \eqref{eq:m0} with its joint household extension \eqref{eq:m0-joint}; the count laws \eqref{eq:m1}--\eqref{eq:m1ol}; the budget law \eqref{eq:m2}; the duration law \eqref{eq:m3}; the placement law \eqref{eq:m4} in both its utility and regret forms; the tour-mode laws \eqref{eq:m5m} (with the logsum linkage \eqref{eq:m5m-ls}) and \eqref{eq:m5m-lc} for the latent-class mixture; and the destination law \eqref{eq:m5d}, applied unchanged at trip level with detour-feasible choice sets \eqref{eq:c-detour}. With case $i$ (a tour for Stage~5), alternative $j$, and attribute $k$, let $V_{ij}=\mathbf{x}_{ij}(G)'\boldsymbol{\theta}$ denote the selected linear predictor of each law (Box--Cox/log transforms absorbed in $\mathbf{x}$; $\mathbf{x}$ draws on person attributes $\mathbf{z}_n$, household attributes $\mathbf{z}^H_h$, size $S_j$, skims, and person$\times$zone interactions from \Cref{tab:notation}). The crash program (C0) contributes \eqref{eq:c0}--\eqref{eq:crash-od}. Every equation is estimated by the penalised inner MLE of \eqref{eq:p2} on its frame $\mathcal{D}_{s,k}$; the outer search chooses $(f,G)$ per block subject to \eqref{eq:c-family}--\eqref{eq:c-refine} plus schedule feasibility \eqref{eq:c-anchor}--\eqref{eq:c-detour} in simulation.

\paragraph{(P2) Full activity-based specification search (master program).}
Index stages $s\in\mathcal{S}=\{0,\ldots,5\}$ (estimation stages; Stage~6 is a deterministic transform with no free parameters and enters only through validation metrics) and, within each stage, estimation segments $k\in\mathcal{K}_s$ (e.g.\ purpose$\times$person-type cells, tour segments) with $n_{s,k}\geq 50$ observations. Stage~5 carries three model blocks --- tour mode, tour destination, and trip destination --- indexed $b\in\mathcal{B}=\{0,1,2,3,4,5m,5d,5b\}$ with admissible family sets $\mathcal{F}_b$ below (5d is tour-level, 5b trip-level; see Table~\ref{tab:decisions}). The program is bilevel: an outer mixed-integer program over specification decisions, with an inner penalised maximum-likelihood fit per stage--segment. \emph{Outer decision variables:} (i) binary covariate-inclusion genes $\mathbf{g}_s\in\{0,1\}^{m_s}$ over the stage candidate pool $V_s$ ($m_s=|V_s|$, covering $\mathbf{z}_n$/$\mathbf{z}^H_h$/size/skim slices); (ii) binary random-parameter status genes $\mathbf{r}_s\in\{0,1\}^{m_s}$ where eligible (fixed vs.\ Normal mixing, greedy Halton-draw toggle; Stage-5 level-of-service distribution genes) plus, for the F5 LC arm, latent-class count $K$ and membership genes $\boldsymbol{\psi}$ (which $\mathbf{z}_n$ enter $\pi_q$, nested vs.\ flat per class, shared $\mu$); (iii) functional-form selectors $\mathbf{y}_b\in\{0,1\}^{|\mathcal{F}_b|}$, one-hot over block $b$'s admissible families (for 5m: kernel $\times$ \{single-class, LatentClass$(K)$\} $\times$ PLC, \eqref{eq:m5m}--\eqref{eq:m5m-lc}). \emph{Notation:} $\mathcal{I}_s$/$\mathcal{E}_s$ are forced inclusions/exclusions; $\mathcal{C}_s$ the collinearity groups; $\mathcal{B}_s$ the behavioural-minimum groups; $\underline{m}_s,\overline{m}_s$ the feature-count bounds; $\Delta_s$ the maximum Hamming moves per perturbation; $\alpha$ the significance level; $\lambda_{\mathrm{JS}}$ the aggregate-fidelity weight; $\kappa>0$ the ACDC spatial-decay rate; $\varepsilon>0$ a small constant avoiding $\log 0$;