\emph{Inner variables:} $\boldsymbol{\theta}_{s,k}(\mathbf{g}_s,\mathbf{r}_s,\mathbf{y}_b)$ fitted by penalised MLE (elastic net held through convergence, removed before inference) subject to sign/box bounds \eqref{eq:c-sign} (incl.\ $c_{\mathrm{crash}}\le 0$, $\beta_{\mathrm{comp}}=0$ if $c_s=0$).
\paragraph{(P2) Objective: total BIC across all stages.} The master program minimises the sum-total BIC over \emph{every} stage $s\in\mathcal{S}=\{0,\dots,5\}$ and \emph{every} segment $k\in\mathcal{K}_s$, plus an aggregate-fidelity regulariser:
\begin{equation}
\begin{aligned}
\min_{\{\mathbf{g}_s,\mathbf{r}_s,\mathbf{y}_b,K,\boldsymbol{\psi},
\mathbf{a}_s,c_s\}}\quad
&\sum_{s\in\mathcal{S}}\sum_{k\in\mathcal{K}_s}
\Bigl[\mathrm{BIC}_{s,k}
+\lambda_{\mathrm{JS}}\mathrm{JSD}_{s,k}\Bigr].
\end{aligned}
\label{eq:p2}
\end{equation}
\begin{equation}
\mathrm{BIC}_{s,k}=-2\hat\ell_{s,k}(\boldsymbol{\theta}_{s,k};\mathbf{g}_s,\mathbf{r}_s,\mathbf{y}_b)+k_{s,k}\ln n_{s,k},\qquad \hat\ell_{s,k}=\max_{\boldsymbol{\theta}}\ell_{s,k},
\label{eq:p2-bic}
\end{equation}
with $\hat\ell_{s,k}$ the maximised penalised log-likelihood on frame $\mathcal{D}_{s,k}$ ($n_{s,k}\ge 50$ obs.), $k_{s,k}$ the number of free parameters priced (counts toward complexity), and $n_{s,k}$ the segment sample size. $\mathrm{JSD}_{s,k}$ is the Jensen--Shannon divergence between predicted and observed destination-zone shares on a fixed-seed within-segment hold-out split, weighted by $\lambda_{\mathrm{JS}}$, penalising specs that fit in-sample yet collapse the aggregate distribution. Total BIC is the model-selection criterion: $-2\hat\ell$ rewards fit, $k\ln n$ penalises complexity, summed so a gene is kept only if it pays across the whole pipeline. The SparseEA-AGDS engine implements \eqref{eq:p2} through the equivalent per-observation mean fitness $\overline{-\mathrm{BIC}/n}$ (same ordering up to fixed positive stage weights, used for cross-stage numerical comparability), with the significance constraints \eqref{eq:c-sig} enforced by exact penalty ($\mathrm{SigPen}$) plus repair.
