Family and set moves enter (P2) through \eqref{eq:c-nhood} with the acceptance rule $\Delta\mathrm{BIC}<-2$ \emph{and} improved validation: PLC mode captivity (captive masses over at most two modes per segment); M3 schedule-constrained destination sets (past-conditioned on placed times, home-anchored); ML consideration (future). The ML arm follows the learned-set literature:
preference-ranked sets \citep{Phan2022NewApproach}, variational-autoencoder
implicit perception \citep{Yao2022VAE,Yao2020DataDriven}, including work-destination
VAE sets \citep{Haghi2026VAEWork}, and ML consideration predictors
\citep{Volakakis2025IntegratingChoice}. Rejected arms leave the specification unchanged, so
every reported refinement demonstrably reduces error against (P0).

The paper's comparison estimand is therefore
$\Delta\mathrm{Err}=\mathrm{Err}(P0)-\mathrm{Err}(P2)$ evaluated on held-out
and validation metrics --- per-observation BIC, McFadden $\rho^2$,
destination-share MAE/JSD with top-25 overlap, post-calibration mode-share
gaps, and trip-length distribution error --- with the in-sample limitation
stated in Discussion applying equally to both arms.

