Two construction choices matter for the utility interpretation. First, exposure accumulates along the single shortest path with no route-choice model, so the skim is exposure on the most direct route rather than an expectation over alternatives. Second, the skim holds \emph{total} expected crashes along the path, not a rate; distance and time enter utilities separately, so the estimated crash coefficient captures marginal disutility of route-accumulated crashes conditional on time and distance, and because longer paths mechanically accumulate more crashes, the negative estimates are conservative. Log and per-kilometre variants are supplied to the search as alternative functional forms.

%\paragraph{Worked example: one tour through the safety chain.} To make the propagation concrete, consider a work tour by a full-time worker resident in SA2 \texttt{301011002} commuting to SA2 \texttt{301011001} (both from the first row of \Cref{tab:od_sample}): the distance-weighted shortest path is $16.1343$\,km and accumulates $52.0110$ Empirical-Bayes expected crashes along its links, so the destination layer prices $\log(1+\mathrm{CRASH}_{jk})=\log(53.01)=3.97$ \emph{net of} $\log$\,distance via the orthogonalisation \eqref{eq:ortho-dest} --- only the crash variation that is not trip length reaches the utility. The same tour's mode block reads the mode-specific exposure $S^{(m)}_{ni}$ \eqref{eq:mode} at the sampled set (20 zones, Manski--Lerman-corrected), and the estimated logsum $\mathrm{LS}(n,j)$ \eqref{eq:m5m-ls} carries the mode-level crash disutility into the destination utility \eqref{eq:dest}; in the latent-class case the class-averaged variant \eqref{eq:m5m-ls-lc} substitutes automatically. Upstream, the participation layer has already seen the home-zone crash-accessibility index, which values reachable destinations by their accumulated crash exposure. The counterfactual of \eqref{eq:cf} simply rescales $52.0110\to 41.6088$ (a 20\% reduction) and re-prices both layers --- this is the entire mechanism by which a network intervention enters behaviour.

