\paragraph{Ethics and privacy.}
All human-participant data in this study enter as de-identified survey microdata supplied under licence by the Queensland Department of Transport and Main Roads; identifiers are stripped upstream of estimation and no re-identification is attempted or possible within the released fields. The 3.8-million-person synthetic population is generated from ABS census tables --- aggregate demographic and dwelling distributions by SA2, not individual records --- and therefore contains no real individuals; zone-level outputs and flows are reproducible summary statistics. Model coefficients, diagnostics, and code artifacts derived from the survey never expose record-level observations, and the published archive ships synthetic-data proofs rather than raw diary extracts.

