\subsection{Held-out validation: fit, transfer, and aggregate recovery}
\label{sec:holdout}

All estimated quantities in this paper are validated on data that took no part in selecting the specification. Two splits are used, both at the person level and stratified on estimation segment: a \emph{random} split (70/30, fixed seed) measuring in-population generalisation, and a \emph{temporal} split (earlier diary waves for selection, the latest for evaluation) measuring temporal transfer, which is the harder test for a model whose purpose is forecasting. Metrics are reported per stage and per segment in \Cref{tab:holdout}: out-of-sample log-likelihood and McFadden $\rho^2$ for the choice models; mean absolute error and Jensen--Shannon divergence of destination-zone shares with top-25 zone overlap; mode-share MAE; and, for the non-choice stages, count MAE (Stage~1), budget and duration calibration error (Stages~2--3), and six-period placement accuracy (Stage~4). No selection-side quantity --- BIC, in-sample $\rho^2$, convergence trajectory --- appears in this table by construction, because it cannot be a validation figure.

